# Project Intelligence - LGD Owocowy Szlak Products Map

## Critical Project Patterns

### 1. Data Structure Pattern
**Pattern**: Wszystkie dane biznesowe w `src/img/1/data.json`
**Why**: Single source of truth, łatwa edycja bez zmian w kodzie
**Impact**: Dodawanie nowych biznesów = edit JSON + dodaj assets
**Never**: Hardcode business data w TypeScript
**New**: Pole `images[]` dla galerii zdjęć (array of paths)

### 2. Service Layer Architecture 🆕
**Pattern**: App → Services → Components
**Structure**:
- `App.ts` - główny controller z orchestration
- `services/MapService.ts` - zarządzanie Leaflet map
- `services/CardService.ts` - zarządzanie kartami biznesów
- `components/` - reusable UI components
**Why**: Separation of concerns, testability, reusability
**Never**: Mix business logic w components

### 3. Component Pattern 🆕
**Pattern**: Self-contained UI components (Card, Carousel, Lightbox)
**Structure**: constructor → render → attachEventListeners
**Why**: Reusability, encapsulation, clear responsibility
**Example**: `Card` tworzy HTML + obsługuje events + integruje Carousel

### 4. Fixed Width Design Philosophy  
**Pattern**: Stała szerokość 665px (brak responsywności mobile)
**Why**: Dedykowane do embedowania w konkretnym kontekście
**Impact**: Wszelkie zmiany muszą uwzględniać fixed width
**Note**: To celowa decyzja, nie bug

### 5. Asset Organization
**Pattern**: Wszystkie zasoby w `src/img/1/`
- Icons: `*.svg` (8 typów dla kategorii)
- Photos: `*.webp` (optimized)
- Multiple images per business: `business_name_1.webp`, `_2.webp`, etc.
- Data: `data.json`
- Styles: `map-style.scss` (legacy) → `main.scss` (new)

### 6. Build Entry Point
**Pattern**: `src/js/map.ts` inicjalizuje `App.ts` który jest głównym controller
**Import Chain**: map.ts → App.ts → Services → Components → types/Point → data.json
**Never**: Zmieniaj entry point bez update webpack.config.js

### 7. Color Coding System
**Pattern**: Każdy biznes ma pole `color` (hex)
**Usage**: Border-color w kartach, tekst w nagłówkach
**Standard**: `#f39000` (pomarańczowy) dla większości
**Impact**: Spójna kolorystyka według kategorii

## Code Conventions

### TypeScript Style
```typescript
// ✅ Good: Defensive programming
const htmlImage = !!image 
  ? `<img src=${image}>` 
  : "";

// ✅ Good: Early return guards
if (!mapContainer) {
  return;
}

// ✅ Good: Descriptive names
generateAddressesHTML()  // not genAddr()

// 🆕 Good: Class-based services
class MapService {
  constructor(containerId: string) {}
  public addMarker(point: Point): Marker {}
}

// 🆕 Good: Private methods in classes
private createCardElement(): HTMLElement {}
```

### HTML Generation
```typescript
// ✅ Good: Template literals dla HTML
`<div class="container">${content}</div>`

// ✅ Good: Conditional rendering
${condition ? `<element>` : ""}

// 🆕 Good: Component-based rendering
const cardElement = document.createElement('div');
cardElement.innerHTML = `...`;
return cardElement;

// ❌ Bad: innerHTML z untrusted data (nie używane w projekcie)
```

### Event Handling
```typescript
// ✅ Good: Named functions dla głównych handlers
function zoomToPoint(event: LeafletEvent) { }

// ✅ Good: Arrow functions dla inline
marker.addEventListener('click', (e) => { })

// 🆕 Good: Event delegation in components
private attachEventListeners(): void {
  this.container.querySelectorAll('.thumbnail')
    .forEach(thumb => thumb.addEventListener('click', ...));
}

// 🆕 Good: Keyboard event handling
document.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {
  if (event.key === 'Escape') this.close();
});
```

### Component Pattern
```typescript
// 🆕 Good: Component structure
class Component {
  private container: HTMLElement;
  
  constructor() {
    this.container = this.render();
    this.attachEventListeners();
  }
  
  private render(): HTMLElement { }
  private attachEventListeners(): void { }
  public getElement(): HTMLElement { return this.container; }
}
```

## Project-Specific Quirks

### 1. Retry Logic for DOM Readiness 🆕
**Current**: App constructor ma 100ms retry logic
**Why**: Ensure map element ma proper dimensions przed init Leaflet
**Location**: `App.ts`, constructor
**Impact**: Rozwiązuje race condition przy ładowaniu

### 2. Carousel Thumbnail Limit
**Current**: Max 3 thumbnails visible + "+X more" indicator
**Why**: UI design decision, prevents overflow
**Location**: `Carousel.ts`, maxVisible = 3
**Impact**: Więcej zdjęć = scrolling przez arrows

### 3. Lightbox Fullscreen Overlay
**Current**: Click overlay to close (w dodatku do ESC i close button)
**Why**: Common UX pattern dla modal/lightbox
**Location**: `Lightbox.ts`, attachEventListeners
**Impact**: Multiple ways to close enhance UX

### 4. Leaflet Version Mismatch
**package.json**: 1.6.0
**CDN**: 1.7.1  
**Status**: Działa, ale niespójne - do sync'u
**Fix**: Update package.json OR CDN link

### 5. Legend Position Change
**Old**: bottom-left
**New**: bottom-right
**Why**: Prawdopodobnie lepsze UX
**Location**: `MapService.ts`, createLegend position

### 6. Webpack CopyPlugin Duplicate
**Current**: Dwa osobne CopyPlugin dla tego samego source
**Status**: Działa ale redundant
**Fix**: Merge do jednego

## Development Workflow

### Adding New Business Point
1. Edit `src/img/1/data.json`
2. Add object with ALL required fields:
   ```json
   {
     "color": "#f39000",
     "latitude": 51.xxx,
     "longitude": 21.xxx,
     "name": "Nazwa",
     "addresses": ["Adres"],
     "emails": ["email"] or null,
     "phoneNumbers": ["+48xxx"] or null,
     "product": "kategoria",
     "image": "./img/1/file.webp" or null,
     "images": ["./img/1/file_1.webp", "./img/1/file_2.webp"] or [],
     "facebook": "url" or null,
     "webpage": "url" or null,
     "icon": "./img/1/icon.svg",
     "legendName": "kategoria",
     "legendSubName": "Wyświetlana nazwa",
     "description": "Pełny opis..."
   }
   ```
3. Add SVG icon if new category
4. Add WebP photos - multiple if gallery needed
5. Run `npm run start` to test
6. Check: marker, popup, legend, card, carousel (if multiple images), lightbox

### Running Development
```bash
npm run start  # Port 4000
# Check http://localhost:4000
```

### Building for Production
```bash
npm run build
# Output in dist/
# Deploy entire dist/ folder
```

## Optimization Opportunities

### High Value, Medium Effort
1. **Lazy Loading Images**: Intersection Observer dla kart
   - Benefit: ~2-3MB savings initial load
   - Implementation: ~8h
   - Risk: Low

2. **Error Handling**: Try-catch + fallbacks
   - Benefit: Better UX
   - Implementation: ~4h
   - Risk: Low

### Medium Value, High Effort
1. **Mobile Responsiveness**: Redesign dla mobile
   - Benefit: Wider audience
   - Implementation: ~2-3 days
   - Risk: Medium (może konflikt z embed context)

2. **CMS Integration**: Backend dla content management
   - Benefit: Non-tech updates
   - Implementation: ~1-2 weeks
   - Risk: High (architecture change)

## Known Technical Debt

### Priority Order
1. Leaflet version sync (2h, low risk)
2. Remove jQuery types (30min, zero risk)
3. Webpack CopyPlugin cleanup (1h, low risk)
4. Clarify popup close behavior (1h, low risk)

### Don't Touch Unless Necessary
- Module structure (Point, utils, map)
- Data JSON schema
- SCSS architecture
- Webpack loaders

## Testing Checklist

### After Any Change:
- [ ] `npm run build` succeeds
- [ ] All 25 markers render
- [ ] Legend shows all items (grouped by category)
- [ ] Legend clicks zoom correctly
- [ ] Popups show correct data
- [ ] All 25 cards render below map
- [ ] 🆕 Carousels show thumbnails (dla biznesów z multiple images)
- [ ] 🆕 Carousel arrows navigate correctly
- [ ] 🆕 Lightbox opens on thumbnail click
- [ ] 🆕 Lightbox keyboard navigation works (←, →, ESC)
- [ ] 🆕 Lightbox counter shows correct X/Y
- [ ] Contact links work (tel:, mailto:, https:)
- [ ] Images load correctly
- [ ] Footer displays properly

### Before Commit:
- [ ] No TypeScript errors
- [ ] No console errors in browser
- [ ] dist/ builds cleanly
- [ ] Test in Chrome/Firefox/Safari

## Communication Patterns

### With Client (LGD)
- **Language**: Polish
- **Focus**: User impact, business value
- **Avoid**: Technical jargon
- **Emphasize**: EU funding context

### With Users (Tourists)
- **Assumption**: Desktop/laptop users primarily
- **Goal**: Easy discovery of local businesses
- **Priority**: Clear information, working links

### With Team
- **Language**: Polish/English mix
- **Focus**: Technical accuracy
- **Tools**: Git, VS Code
- **Standards**: TypeScript, webpack, modern practices

